      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I second this.\n\nI sometimes run into the issue of people touching me without my consent. Often it's not in an inappropriate way, but still in a way that I'm not comfortable with from people I don't know.\n\nThe current implementation of \"Personal Space\" feels like it treats the symptoms, but not the actual cause. It does not stop people from invading your personal space, it hides the interaction from you visually, but you still know it's happening. For everyone else, the interaction is still taking place as normal.\n\nI would love for this feature to be toggle-able to everyone or non-friends, perhaps as an extension to the current avatar interactions system.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
